cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SlipSurfaceIQ LE in your work, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Please also cite the limit equilibrium methods you used (for example
  Bishop 1955, Spencer 1967, Morgenstern and Price 1965).
type: software
title: "SlipSurfaceIQ LE: 2D limit equilibrium slope stability analysis with a desktop CAD interface"
abstract: >-
  SlipSurfaceIQ LE is an open-source Python program for two-dimensional limit
  equilibrium slope stability analysis of soil and rock slopes, cuts and
  embankments. It implements the classic methods of slices (Ordinary, Bishop
  simplified, Janbu simplified and corrected, Corps of Engineers, Lowe-Karafiath,
  Spencer and Morgenstern-Price/GLE) for circular and non-circular slip surfaces,
  linear and non-linear strength models (Mohr-Coulomb, Hoek-Brown,
  Barton-Bandis, power-law, undrained and SHANSEP), groundwater, pseudo-static
  seismic loading, tension cracks, external loads and reinforcement, a global
  critical-surface search, a bilingual (English/Turkish) desktop interface and
  PDF reporting.
